  "reasoning": "According to historical Congressional Research Service (CRS) and Pew Research Center records, the last time Congress enacted all of its regular appropriations bills before the start of the fiscal year (October 1) was for Fiscal Year 1997 (enacted in late September 1996). Since the passage of the Congressional Budget Act of 1974, Congress has only enacted all regular appropriations bills on time in four fiscal years: FY 1977, FY 1989, FY 1995, and FY 1997. Since FY 1997, Congress has consistently relied on continuing resolutions or omnibus spending packages enacted well after the October 1 deadline, meaning a complete budget has not been passed on time since then.",
